\end{comment}

Here we used Lemma \ref{lemma: coev lemma} in the third equality while the fourth is obvious ($P_{X,X}$ is just a permutation isomorphism). Since $P_{X,X}$ and $\overrightarrow{\text{coev}}_X^{\otimes N}$ have $\mathbb{Q}$-coefficients and $(\iota_X\otimes \text{id}_X)^{\otimes N}$ has coefficients in $q^{2\alpha N}\mathbb{Q}(q)$, from what we said about $B'_0$ it follows that $B'$
has coefficients with $\text{max-deg}_{q^{-2\alpha}}<N, \text{max-deg}_{q^{2\alpha}}\leq N$. Summing up, we get
\begin{figure}[H]
    \includegraphics[width=13cm]{proof-final-step.pdf}
\end{figure}
\begin{comment}







\end{comment}
\noindent and $B:=B'+\overline{F}(Z^{low},X)$ has coefficients with $\text{max-deg}_{q^{-2\alpha}}< N, \text{max-deg}_{q^{2\alpha}}\leq N$ since both $B'$ and $\overline{F}(Z^{low},X)$ have this property. This proves $(a)$.
\medskip

We now prove $(c)$. Applying $\text{id}_{V_{\alpha}}\otimes \overleftarrow{\text{ev}}_{V_{\alpha}}^{2N}$ to (\ref{eq prop: FTX in terms of coev + B}) and using Proposition \ref{prop: Seifert formula} (on the LHS) gives $$LG(L;q,q^{2\alpha+1})\cdot\text{id}_{V_{\alpha}}=c(q,q^{\alpha})\cdot\text{id}_{V_{\alpha}}+(\text{id}_{V_{\alpha}}\otimes \overleftarrow{\text{ev}}_{V_{\alpha}}^{2N})\circ (B\otimes \text{id}_{V_{\alpha}}).$$
Since the coefficients of $B$ satisfy $\text{max-deg}_{q^{-2\alpha}}<N$ from $(a)$ it follows that $LG(L)$ and $c(q,q^{\alpha})$ have the same coefficient of $q^{-2\alpha N}$. But since $LG(L)$ and $c(q,q^{\alpha})$ have the same symmetry property, namely invariance under $p\mapsto p^{-1}$ if $p=q^{2\alpha+1}$ (since $\kappa(\alpha)$ does as noted in Remark \ref{remark: symmetry of kappa alpha} and $c(q,q^{\alpha})$ is a power of $\kappa(\alpha)$ up to a coefficient in $\mathbb{Q}(q)$), it follows that $LG(L)$ and $c(q,q^{\alpha})$ have the same coefficient of $q^{2\alpha N}$ as well, therefore proving $(c)$. From this, it follows that the coefficients of $$(LG(L;q,q^{2\alpha+1})-c(q,q^{\alpha}))\cdot\text{id}_{V_{\alpha}}=\text{cl}(B)$$
satisfy $\text{max-deg}_{q^{\pm 2\alpha}}<N$ which implies $(b)$.
